<title>ITALY: Italy September producer prices rose 0.2 pct. [CORRECTED 08:38 GMT]</title>
<headline>Italy September producer prices rose 0.2 pct. [CORRECTED 08:38 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian industrial producer prices rose 0.2 percent year-on-year in September, the national statistics institute ISTAT said in a statement.</p>
<p>    PRODUCER PRICES	   Sept 96    Aug 96    Sept 95</p>
<p>    Year/year change	+0.2 pct	0.0 pct     +8.7 pct</p>
<p>    Month/month change    +0.2 pct     +0.1 pct     +0.1 pct</p>
<p>(corrects Month/month change for Sept 96 from +0.1 to +0.2)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990=100)  124.1	 123.8	  123.9</p>
<p>Istat gave the following general breakdown:</p>
<p>				  Mo/Mo change (%)    Yr/Yr change (%)</p>
<p>    Consumer goods	     0.0		    +1.5</p>
<p>    Investment goods	   0.0		    +4.2</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods	+0.6		    +1.1</p>
<p>It gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown:</p>
<p>    Sector			    mo/mo (%)	     yr/yr (%)</p>
<p>    Energy products		 +1.6		     +3.2</p>
<p>    Minerals and metals	   -0.4		    -10.5</p>
<p>    Non-metal minerals	     0.0		     +0.3</p>
<p>    Pharamceutical/cemicals     +0.2		     -4.1</p>
<p>    Metal works		     +0.1		     +2.2</p>
<p>    Cars and parts		   0.0		     +5.9</p>
<p>    Food, drink and tobacco     +0.1		     +1.1</p>
<p>    Clothing, leather goods	0.0		     +0.7</p>
<p>    Other goods			0.0		     -2.2</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
